From 69f23d4c694dc0077145ec7fdaee3355f89dfe8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:13:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): supervisor-request archive op for orphaned
 unstarted descendants [daveey]

A worker had no supported route to cancel a card its task did not create
directly: standing card S created owner B, B created QA card C, B was archived
when its PR closed, and C sat TODO with nobody able to cancel it.
kanban_archive refused (C's creator is B, not S), kanban_block(kind=assignment)
answered no_capable_supervisor (same profile), and the supervisor-request
schema had no archive op, so only an unscoped operator could clean it up
(Ask Eve QA t_01a1947dae56913a).

New op {op: archive, task_id}, its own request family, executed by the
existing non-worker supervisor executor through kanban_db.archive_task. Scope:
the target's creator chain must reach the requester within 3 hops through
cards that are all done or archived (a live intermediate owns it); cards the
requester created directly are refused with a pointer to kanban_archive; self,
foreign, unknown, done/archived and claimed/running targets are refused. The
executor re-checks scope and target state at execution, records the request id
on the archived event, and a redelivered request reports already_applied.
kanban_archive's worker scope is unchanged.
